:''Not to be confused with the [[Citadel]]s, [[Infernal Tower]] or [[Golden Tower]].''
The '''Heavenly Tower''' (風雲にゃんこ塔, ''Fūun Nyanko Tō'', '''Wind and Cloud Cat Tower''') is an event added in the [[Version 6.2 Update]]. It usually comes around during the [[Anniversary]], but otherwise has no known schedule. All of the rewards reset on every appearance. The Cat Units unlocked from [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]], and [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] are only obtainable once from the [[Catnip Challenges|Missions]] screen. As of [[Version 11.0 Update|Version 11.0]], the event has a checkpoint system, allowing you to restart from a higher tower floor than before and replay previous stages for their rewards as well. Completing [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]] will grant the player access to the [[Infernal Tower]].

Ports for The Battle Cats would eventually receive this event at a much later date. For [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou]], its one and only appearance was from September 18, 2018 to October 2, 2018. It was later added to [[The Battle Cats Unite!|The Battle Cats Unite]] via an update, [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Version 1.0.6]], and can be accessed when clearing [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] in the [[Empire of Cats]] chapter. After 30 days from a floor's initial clear, rewards are reset and can be cleared again. Specifically in the Nintendo Switch version, clearing [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 10|Floor 10]] makes [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stages]] playable and are permanent.
{{Map Stars|4095}}

==Overview==
The Heavenly Tower contains 50 stages, called '''Floors''' (階 ''Kai''), with a wide variety of enemies including [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, [[:Category:Enemy Cats|Enemy Cats]], [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]] and even [[:Category:Event Enemies|event enemies]] from monthly and annual events. After completing a floor for the first time, the player will receive gifts including [[Battle Items]], [[Catseye]]s, [[Catfruit]], [[Cat Capsule|Tickets]], [[Gamatoto Expedition|Catamins]], XP, [[Ototo Corps|Materials]] and [[Leadership]]s along with [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]], [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]] and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] upon defeating [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|their]] [[Mystic Mask Yulala|respective]] [[Master Uril (Enemy)|counterparts]] on the 30th, 40th and 50th floors respectively, via the [[Catnip Challenges]] feature.

