==Recommendations==
*Spam to win works for most of the early stages.
*Most of the stages can't be cheesed.
*Completing every 10th floor grants 11 (1+1+3+3+3) total Rare Cat Tickets. Completing the whole tower can also give 9+ Cat Tickets that can usually be exchanged for an extra Rare Cat Ticket, as well as [[Gamatoto Expedition|Catamins]], a lot of [[Catfruit]] (five each of the basic Catfruit Seeds, an additional three base Catfruit of each basic type and six Epic Catfruit) and many more rewards, making it worthwhile to go through the tower every time it appears, even if already completed once.

===Recommended Cats===
A list of all cats the player should have in possession to go through all 50 floors.
*[[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]]: 20 or higher for the first few stages, 20+10 for floors 15~19, and 20+50 generally for most floors beyond that.
*[[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]]: 30~40 including some of the purchasable cats that can be part of [[Cat Combo|Combos]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] and [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] (also for Combos). [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]], [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Heroic Musashi]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Minka]] and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] should also be taken into consideration if no [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] alternatives can cover their roles.
*[[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]]: [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]], [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]].
*[[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cats]]: High-level [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] (preferably with [[Talents]]), [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Catway (Super Rare Cat)|Drone Cat]] and the [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]] (notable are [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera]]).
*Recommended [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]]: [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]], [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]], [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]/[[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-00]], [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Anubis the Unblemished]], a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]], another [[Critical Hit]]ter, a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cat]] and a general attacker. Ubers are not required to beat the Heavenly Tower, but they make everything easier nonetheless.

===Boss Skip/Speedrun===
*Floor 22: Flying Ninja Cat and hordes of Brollows can be skipped by stacking Ms. Signs to stop the boss from appearing or using [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]] to destroy the base after killing the first Brollow.
*Floor 25: Heavy Assault C.A.T. boss fight and Berserkory can be skipped by using Awakened Bahamut Cat and other high speed/DPS units like Can Can Cat or Maglev Cat reach and destroy the enemy base early. More firepower, Combos or a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] would also be needed.
*Floor 30: Awakened Bahamut can be abused to clip through Hermit Cat and destroy the base. However, this requires extremely precise timing.
*Floors 30, 40 and 50 can all be cheesed using a combination of [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] and the Tourist Cat to permafreeze the respective bosses. This requires some precise timing and luck, which will always result in many attempts being required. It is, therefore, generally easier to beat these stages the intended way unless otherwise specified.

