==Trivia==
*The Heavenly Tower is a direct reference to [[wikia:dragonball:Korin Tower|Korin Tower]] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Ball|Dragon Ball]]'', having a similar appearance, an old but deceptively powerful [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|martial artist cat]] who even looks like [[wikia:dragonball:Korin|Korin]], and a [[Infernal Tower|dark counterpart]] equivalent to [[wikia:dragonball:Chocolay Tower|Chocolay Tower]].
*The event poster shown whenever Heavenly Tower appears is seemingly a parody of [https://pbs.twimg.com/media/EPMn_KgUEAAIZ5x.jpg this artwork] for ''[[wikipedia:The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild|The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild]]''.
*Heavenly Tower's Japanese name, Fūun Nyanko Tō (風雲にゃんこ塔, "Wind and Cloud Cat Tower") may be a reference to ''Fūun! Takeshi-jō'' (風雲!たけし城, "Turbulence! Takeshi Castle"), the Japanese name of the game show ''[[wikipedia:Takeshi's Castle|Takeshi's Castle]]''. 風雲 ''Fūun'' can mean "wind and cloud" or "turbulence".
*Floors 31~40 were added in [[Version 6.7 Update|Version 6.7]], and Floors 41~50 were added in [[Version 9.6 Update|Version 9.6]].
*Heavenly Tower was the first event map to be extended with more stages.
**Technically, the [[XP Stage|Weekend Stage]], which predates Heavenly Tower, originally only had 3 stages, but the extension was done by creating a new map rather than modifying the existing one.
*[[Heavenly Tower/Floor 43|Floor 43]] being the first and only Heavenly Tower floor to have [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] may be a reference to how the 43rd [[Stories of Legend]] sub-chapter, [[Area 22]], is the first sub-chapter to have Starred Aliens.
*[[Heavenly Tower/Floor 48|Floor 48]] having [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]] may be a reference to how [[Teacher Bun Bun]], whom Mecha-Bun is a variant of, debuts in [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|stage 48]] of [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3.
*Even after obtaining the Heavenly Tower's [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]], their [[Catnip Challenges]] continue to reappear every time their respective stages are beaten during subsequent Heavenly Tower events, but claiming them will provide no rewards.
*After [[Infernal Tower]] was added, Heavenly Tower's event poster was updated to have another tower that can be vaguely seen off to the right.
*Heavenly Tower would be part of an update that features new levels, a first for [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], taking 1,667 days since its release in Japan.

